{
  "annotations": [
    {
      "start_time": 0,
      "end_time": 0,
      "annotation": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "For his performance—called “Poésie guerrière”—Montrealer Jack V starts off by singing while shaving with an electric razor."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "tags": [
        {
          "category": "Alan Lord Commentary",
          "tag": "Event Description"
        }
      ],
      "uuid": "83e64fbe-30df-4d83-9e8f-e0d794515fba"
    },
    {
      "start_time": 61,
      "end_time": 61,
      "annotation": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "He says \"sept ans d'malheur!\" (seven years bad luck!) and smashes a mirror"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "tags": [
        {
          "category": "Alan Lord Commentary",
          "tag": "Event Description"
        }
      ],
      "uuid": "60c87ef8-d87f-494c-b316-3b64f683d974"
    },
    {
      "start_time": 89,
      "end_time": 89,
      "annotation": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "The music we hear faintly in the background is the song Hospitality by Sparks"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "tags": [
        {
          "category": "Alan Lord Commentary",
          "tag": "Event Description"
        }
      ],
      "uuid": "7c03390a-101e-4b3f-bbf5-14425398a692"
    },
    {
      "start_time": 156,
      "end_time": 156,
      "annotation": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "He then stripped down to the waist, thus revealing the war paint on his body. He started dancing, prancing and swaying in abandon like a wild man."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "tags": [
        {
          "category": "Alan Lord Commentary",
          "tag": "Event Description"
        }
      ],
      "uuid": "abe8b3dc-1e63-4985-8797-4159a5fff6b3"
    },
    {
      "start_time": 275,
      "end_time": 275,
      "annotation": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Jack was a member of the Neoists, and played bass in Monty Cantsin’s First Aid Brigade."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "tags": [
        {
          "category": "Alan Lord Commentary",
          "tag": "Biographical Context"
        }
      ],
      "uuid": "baa85b55-e34d-4c57-997a-a8c642ed2a27"
    },
    {
      "start_time": 431,
      "end_time": 431,
      "annotation": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Festival participants Jack V, Jean-Luc Bonspiel, Jean-Martin Mignault and I later formed Montreal’s seminal agitrock band Vent du Mont Schärr (1986 – 1990)."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "tags": [
        {
          "category": "Alan Lord Commentary",
          "tag": "Biographical Context"
        }
      ],
      "uuid": "f5ffcb78-9f1f-4c5b-9566-8f4364a54eda"
    },
    {
      "start_time": 1008,
      "end_time": 1008,
      "annotation": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "He is joined by a regiment of a half-dozen drummers, one by one—a Post-Punk marching band—martially rat-tatting their snares. Jack was feline and menacing, irresistibly magnetic. This was poetry beyond words, and one of the festival’s highlights."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "tags": [
        {
          "category": "Alan Lord Commentary",
          "tag": "Event Description"
        },
        {
          "category": "Alan Lord Commentary",
          "tag": "Personal Anecdote"
        }
      ],
      "uuid": "a414e607-af25-48ae-803d-fa4a1e308000"
    }
